# The SDR's arrival finishes a bring-up that deferred the radio.
#
# mjh, 2026-10-04: never write "done" when not done.  A bring-up that found no
# SDR installs everything, defers the radio half, and leaves the first-run
# marker at result=awaiting-sdr.  When an RX-888 with firmware loaded (Cypress
# FX3, 04b4:00f1) appears, ask systemd for sigmond-sdr-arrival.service, which
# starts first-run bring-up ONLY when the radio half is owed (awaiting-sdr, or
# no marker yet).  It must not start bring-up directly: a working card
# re-enumerates many times, and a result=retry station would then get a full
# unattended bring-up under it (pre-build review of v3.68, 2026-10-05).
# Fargo is the case: nobody on site, and no reboot coming.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="04b4", ATTR{idProduct}=="00f1", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="sigmond-sdr-arrival.service"
